    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed the two failing tests in the frai-core test suite:\n\n### 1. **Governance module test failure** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`)\n**Issue:** The test imports `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it wasn't being exported from `index.js`.\n\n**Fix:** Added named exports for the governance constants in `src/finetune/index.js`:\n```javascript\nexport { APPROVAL_STATUSES, DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS, GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS, RISK_LEVELS };\n```\n\n### 2. **Evaluation test failure** (`src/eval/index.test.js`)\n**Issue:** The `toxicityMetric` function had an incompatible signature. When called by `runEvaluations` with `(outputs, references)`, the references were incorrectly assigned to the `bannedTerms` parameter, causing false toxicity flags.\n\n**Fix:** Updated the `toxicityMetric` function signature in `src/eval/metrics.js` to match the calling convention:\n```javascript\nexport function toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms) {\n```\n\nBoth fixes are minimal, targeted changes that maintain backward compatibility. All **28 tests now pass** with no test files modified and no scratch files left behind.",
